repository-code: "https://github.com/FaizPalwala/virtual-id-gen"
abstract: >
  A family of synthetic, identity-conditioned face datasets generated via
  InstantID + Juggernaut-XL-v9 from CC0 synthetic SFHQ seed images.  750
  synthetic identities with identity-level split isolation (retain 675 /
  forget 75) and MUFAC-aligned per-image train + holdout subsets, following
  a sequential 15-step forgetting protocol.  Two releases:
  SFHQ-VirtualID-Bench (224x224 aligned crops — 67,500 balanced + 36,064
  imbalanced with a ratio-based 82:41:16 train gradient, both schedules
  uniform and seeded-Poisson) and SFHQ-VirtualID-Raw (1024x1024 portraits,
  75,000 images, JPEG q95 4:4:4, max-size reference).
keywords:
  - synthetic face dataset
  - machine unlearning
  - identity-conditioned generation
  - InstantID
  - Juggernaut-XL-v9
  - SDXL
  - long-tail distribution
